# Files/paths the comment harvest skips (read by
# scripts/devtools/harvest-comments.R, and by update-comments.R when it decides
# whether a block in the edited file is one it is allowed to write).
#
# Same three pattern forms as .docignore, one per line:
#
#   stale/            a trailing "/" means "any path containing this folder"
#   Test*.bas         a pattern with * or ? is matched against the FILE NAME
#   classes/geo/LLGeo.cls   anything else is matched as a substring of the path
#
# A line starting with "#" is a comment. Blank lines are ignored.
# Pass --no-ignore to either script to read every file regardless of this list.

# Dead code kept only until deletion. Its comments still describe interfaces
# that no longer exist, so there is nothing here worth editing by hand.
stale/
